Ray,

My quess is that you are running into an alignment problem!

In the case you give below, the 'short len' is misaligned on an odd byte
boundary.  This might be the cause of the problem...

I know that with DEC/Compaq cc there is a #pragma and also a compiler switch to
assume_unaligned pointers for cases like this.  The code that is generated is
awfull but the end result is the correct value loaded into the register.  I
don't know that the [g]cc equivalent switch is but presume that there is one!

Alternatively, change the code slightly to ensure that the 'mumpspc' pointer is
always incremented by an even number of bytes.  eg.

mumpspc += ( ((cstring*)mumpspc)->len + sizeof(short) + 2 ) & ~1; /* bump pc and round up */

Tony
